      "text": "First, let's find the lengths of the legs of the right triangle. The legs are given as $\\log_4 27$ and $\\log_2 9$. We can use the change of base formula for logarithms to rewrite these expressions in a common base, such as base 10 or base $e$.\n\nRecall that $\\log_b a = \\frac{\\log_c a}{\\log_c b}$ for any positive base $c$.\n\nFor the first leg:\n\\begin{align*}\n\\log_4 27 &= \\frac{\\log_{10} 27}{\\log_{10} 4} \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\log_{10} 27}{\\log_{10} 4^2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\log_{10} 27}{2\\log_{10} 2}.\n\\end{align*}\n\nFor the second leg:\n\\begin{align*}\n\\log_2 9 &= \\frac{\\log_{10} 9}{\\log_{10} 2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\log_{10} 3^2}{\\log_{10} 2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{2\\log_{10} 3}{\\log_{10} 2}.\n\\end{align*}\n\nNow, we can compute the hypotenuse, $h$:\n\\begin{align*}\nh &= (\\log_4 27)^2 + 2^2 \\\\\n&= \\left(\\frac{\\log_{10} 27}{2\\log_{10} 2}\\right)^2 + 2^2 \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\log_{10} 27^2}{4\\log_{10} 2^2} + 4 \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\log_{10} 729}{8\\log_{10} 4} + 4 \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\log_{10} 3^6}{8\\log_{10} 2^2} + 4 \\\\\n&= \\frac{6\\log_{10} 3}{8\\log_{10} 2} + 4 \\\\\n&= \\frac{3\\log_{10} 3}{4\\log_{10} 2} + 4 \\\\\n&= \\frac{3\\log_{10} 3}{4\\log_{10} 2} + 4 \\\\\n&= \\frac{3\\log_{10} 3}{4\\log_{10} 2} + 4.\n\\end{align*}\n\nFinally, we can compute $4^h$:\n\\begin{align*}\n4^h &= 4^h \\\\\n&= 4^{\\frac{3\\log_{10} 3}{4\\log_{10} 2} + 4} \\\\\n&= 4^4 \\cdot 4^{\\frac{3\\log_{10} 3}{4\\log_{10} 2}} \\\\\n&= 256 \\cdot (4^{\\log_{10} 3}/4^{\\log_{10} 2}) \\\\\n&= 256 \\cdot (3/2) \\\\\n&= 912.\n\\end{align*}\n\nSo the final answer is $4^h = \\boxed{912}$. The answer is 912.",
